# TheToDo — optional configuration
#
# Nothing here is required. The app runs with no .env at all: your tasks, notes,
# diary, planner, boosters and SilentBoy are local, and API keys are entered in
# Settings → API keys & connections.
#
# Copy this file to `.env` in the project folder only if you prefer configuring
# something on disk.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Telegram API credentials
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Needed to read the three channels that do not publish a public web preview:
#   https://t.me/DU27T              physics theory
#   https://t.me/DU27BNRe           physics revision
#   https://t.me/RD27PAPERONLINE    combined maths paper
# It is also what lets the reading engine download the PDF and image papers
# teachers attach.
#
# Get api_id / api_hash once from https://my.telegram.org -> API development
# tools. Any app name works; use "TheToDo". These belong to you and are not
# shared with anyone.
#
# You can also paste these into Settings → Telegram API credentials, which is
# usually easier. If both are set, this file wins.
TG_API_ID=
TG_API_HASH=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Reading engine
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The engine binds to a port on the loopback interface only. It is started by the
# app; you never need to run it yourself.
# CLASSRADAR_PORT=5188

# Where the engine keeps its messages, database, Telegram session and downloads.
# Defaults to the app's own data folder, so there is one thing to back up.
# CLASSRADAR_DATA_DIR=

# Uncomment to see the engine's own logging, including the MTProto client's
# connection trace. Off by default, because a background process does not need
# to narrate itself.
# THETODO_DEBUG=1

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# AI API keys
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Prefer the Settings screen: it stores keys per connection, tracks which are
# working or throttled, and rotates between them automatically. Free tiers cap
# requests per key, so adding several keys for one connection is the single most
# effective way to get more done.
#
# Listed here only so you know the names. Do not commit a filled-in copy of this
# file.
#
# GEMINI_API_KEY=      https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=  https://openrouter.ai/keys
# KILO_API_KEY=        https://kilo.ai/docs/gateway
# GROQ_API_KEY=        https://console.groq.com/keys
